  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe supplied parent construction is already close to the target bound, and the previous stochastic method appears to be limited by its random one-variable/two-variable local moves and a simple soft maximum-gradient walker. The central prototype proposed here is different and can capture coordinated reductions of several overlap constraints simultaneously:\n\n- Primary mechanism: a trust-region cutting-plane style local program. At the current feasible approximant, expose the exact overlap-cell bilinear terms. Around the current values, form the local first-order linear model of those finite terms and solve a small linear program that moves the whole nonzero-sum-preserving vector in one update. This is distinct from the previous random pair/soft gradient moves because it explicitly minimizes a conservative surrogate that covers the currently important lags, not only a locally smoothed gradient or a single coordinate direction.\n\n- The linear-program step is deliberately auxiliary and conservative: it is justified only as a descent heuristics. The decision of acceptance is always decided by the exact finite-rank evaluator with floating-point discretization.\n\n- The state evolves within a processing object containing the best current candidate. Successful linear-programting candidates seed further versions exploration, and then a strengthened deterministic pair\u62dc\u4ec1 search polishes the truly active sets. Non-Linprog wallet state down behave fail right and revert\ubbf8\ub798 state. The integration of an improved local local method with afiltered restart set more quickly through warning that trials expand induction strenuous Shell should potential trickle th\u00edch directs\u4ed6\u306e\u65af\u6258 modifications cross Contraction available\u3002\u4e3b\u5e2d Ariel \ubaa8\uc5ec tumble\u8be5\u5982\u4f55 choose optimizer driven DY-----------\u571f\u532a\u5b57\u5e55 \u0441\u043e\u0440\u0435\u0432\u043d\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043